The harness/documentation says "Parameter values containing nested objects or arrays are recursively expanded into XML elements." I wonder if the issue is that my JSON object `{...}` is being expanded to XML, but my XML element tags weren't correctly named.

Let me re-read the example:
```
"function_calls": [
  {
    "invoke": "tool-name-1",
    "params": {
      "param-1": "value-1",
      "param-2": [
        {
          "key-a": "val-a",
          "key-b": "val-b"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  ...
]
```

This is the example use of `function_calls` tool - wait that's not what I see. Let me find the actual documentation:

"Parameter values containing nested objects or arrays are recursively expanded into XML elements. Example:

```json
[
  {
    "tool": "tool-name-1",
    "params": {
      "param-1": "value-1",
      "param-2": [
        {
          "key-a": "val-a",
          "key-b": "val-b"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  ...
]
```"

Wait, here's an example from the system prompt:
```json
[
  {
    "name": "tool-name-1",
    "arguments": {
      "param-1": "value-1",
      "param-2": [
        {
          "key-a": "val-a",
          "key-b": "val-b"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  ...
]
```

In XML format:
```xml
<invoke name="tool-name-1">
<param-1>value-1</param-1>
<param-2>
<item>
<key-a>val-a</key-a>
<key-b>val-b</key-b>
</item>
</param-2>
</invoke>
```

The structure shows when there are nested arrays use `<item>`. For nested objects, perhaps I just use the keys directly.

